description: Unit tests are required for new functionality
alwaysApply: true
---

# Testing protocol

- Add unit tests for new functionality, features, stories, and infra.
- Colocate as `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` next to the unit, or under a nearby `__tests__` folder.
- Test behavior at the unit boundary: pure functions, use-case logic, mappers, validators. Mock I/O (Prisma, Redis, GitHub, fetch).
- Do not add Jest/Vitest/Playwright packages, or change test scripts, without asking.
- If tooling is missing, ask to add a runner (prefer Vitest for this Node/React workspace) and still write the test files.
- Do not finish with “tests left as follow-up” unless the user agreed.
